From d0b36b7dd738f6139e78b2ded66a6fcd7d488b8a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: logdog2325 <loganjayfisher@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 14:04:51 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Desktop: a Pokemon hub, and a PBR launcher to match Android

Mac and Windows had no PBR interface at all -- the Wiimmfi patch has
always been frontend-agnostic (BootManager applies it for any frontend),
so desktop could BOOT PBR but had nothing to set it up with. Add the
launcher: a checklist for the disc (any supported region, with the
in-memory patch explained), the save, and the NAND, plus a Play button.

The save row installs the bundled starter save from Sys/XDNetplay, the
same community save the Android build ships, so the team editor has
something to read instead of waiting for the user to play PBR first.
Desktop ships it already encrypted and copies it verbatim rather than
porting the cipher. It lands in the title directory of the DETECTED disc
region, so a PAL player's save is not filed where only a USA game would
look; a file that is present but the wrong size now says so instead of
showing a green tick; an existing save is only ever replaced through an
explicit confirm, and its backup is never overwritten by a later one.

Also add the hub Android has had: one window that asks XD or PBR and
opens the right launcher. It takes over the launcher-at-startup slot
(same QSettings key, so anyone who turned startup off stays off), and
both launchers remain directly reachable from Tools.
